-- title:
--   μₑ-invariants of a crossing model form the e-fold model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and $\pi \in W$, and assume $W$ is precomplete for the ideal $(\pi)$ and that $\pi$-adic separatedness holds in the form: any $x \in W$ divisible by $\pi^n$ for all $n$ is $0$. Let $e$ be a nonzero natural number, and let $\zeta, \zeta' \in W$ satisfy $\zeta^e = 1$, $\zeta\zeta' = 1$, and $\zeta^m - 1 \in W^{\mathrm{nzd}}$ (a non-zero-divisor) for every $m$ with $0 < m < e$. For $t \in W$ write $R_t$ for the crossing model `UVCrossingModel W t`, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring $W[[X_0, X_1]]$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - t$, and `mk t` for the quotient map. The assertion is that there exist a $W$-algebra homomorphism $\theta \colon R_{\pi^e} \to R_\pi$ and a $W$-algebra automorphism $\delta$ of $R_\pi$ such that: $\theta$ carries the class of any $F \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ to the class of `MvPowerSeries.expand e he F` (substitution of $e$-th powers of the variables); $\theta$ is injective; $\delta$ carries the class of $F$ to the class of `MvPowerSeries.rescale ![ζ, ζ'] F`, i.e. of $F(\zeta X_0, \zeta' X_1)$; and for every $z \in R_\pi$ one has $\delta(z) = z$ if and only if $z$ lies in the range of $\theta$.
--
--   This identifies the ring of invariants of the diagonal $\mu_e$-action $(X_0, X_1) \mapsto (\zeta X_0, \zeta' X_1)$ on the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi)$ with the crossing model $W[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1 - \pi^e)$, embedded via $e$-th powers of the coordinates. It is used in the local analysis of the completed local rings at the nodes of a modular curve, where the width of a crossing is computed after linearising a $\mu_e$-stabiliser; it is cited by [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_algHom_range_eq_fixedPoints_apply_U_apply_V_of_tangent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.exists_algHom_range_eq_fixedPoints_apply_U_apply_V_of_tangent).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_exists_powMap_range_eq_fixedPoints.lean

